Net work done by a gas,

$\begin{array}{ll}\Delta W_{A B}=p \cdot \Delta V=10 \times(2-1)=10 \mathrm{ J}$\\
\Delta W_{B C}=0  $\text{ (as }V=\text{ constant) }
\end{array}$From first law of thermodynamics,
we have, $\Delta Q=\Delta W+\Delta U
\triangle U=0 \quad \text{ (process }A$B C A $\text{$ is cyclic) }Therefore, $\Delta Q=\Delta W_{A B}+\Delta W_{B C}+\Delta W_{C A}
\begin{aligned}
\therefore \quad$\Delta$ W_{C A} & =\left(\Delta$Q-W_{A B}-W_{B C}\right) \\
& =(5-10-0) $\mathrm{J}=-$5 $\mathrm{ J}$
\end{aligned}

